	(text "Memory map: device window = MEM_SEL x 64 KB (ADDR[23:16] = device index,\nADDR[15:0] = offset).  The 74HC688 compares the high byte ADDR[23:16]\nwith MEM_SEL; within a window only the device address pins are decoded.\n00 INPUT_SRAM 01 CONV1_OUT 02 POOL1_OUT 03 CONV2_OUT 04 POOL2_OUT\n05 FC1_OUT 06 FC2_LOGITS\n08 W_CONV1 09 W_CONV2 0A W_FC1 0B W_FC2   (62256, boot-loaded)\n0C..0F bias, 10..13 qparam: reserved, no device fitted\n14/15 LUT0 LO/HI 16/17 LUT1 LO/HI\n18/19 LUT2 LO/HI 1A/1B LUT3 LO/HI\n07 and 1C..1F are unmapped.  6264 uses ADDR[12:0],\n62256 ADDR[14:0], W27C512 ADDR[15:0]."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 520 40 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.15 1.15)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "acfd52d9-55e1-4666-8288-37117c79c268")
	)

	(text "Chip-select decode: 4x 74HC138 decode MEM_SEL[2:0]; the group\nenables are MSEL[4:3].  DEC_EN = ADDR_TAG_OK AND MEM_CE_OK,\nwhere MEM_CE_OK = NOT(MEM_nCE AND NOT LOAD_EN) and\nADDR_TAG_OK = (ADDR[23:16] == {000, MEM_SEL[4:0]}).\nExactly one nCS can be low at a time; unmapped indices select\nnothing.  ADDR[15:0] is a tri-state bus (host U93/U94 or the active\nengine via U44..U49); no 2:1 address multiplexer is used.\nLoad port J1 carries LOAD_DATA/LOAD_EN/LOAD_nWE/nOE and READY pulses;\nADDR[15:0] come from S10 while LOAD_EN=1 and from the active engine's\nC1/C2/FC_ADDR via U44..U49 while LOAD_EN=0; ADDR[23:16] and MEM_SEL come\nfrom S10 (load) or the S11 tag/MEM_SEL buffers (inference).\nLOAD_EN=1 disables the system data buffer and enables the load buffer.\nThe W27C512 LUTs are programmed once on a bench programmer; they have no\nin-system write path because their address pins carry A*B, not ADDR."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 520 90 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.15 1.15)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9401063a-36d4-40fb-a308-59020ad79551")
	)

	(embedded_fonts no)
)
